   $q$Paragraph 1 ends with a question. How does this question help organize the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It begins a list of steps that the town follows every single spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"},{"text":"It shows that the author does not know why the river rises in spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It sets up the rest of the passage, which answers it by explaining the causes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It introduces a comparison between the river in spring and in fall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It sets up the rest of the passage, which answers it by explaining the causes.$q$, $q$The question "What causes this to happen?" is answered right away in paragraph 2: "The main cause is melting snow." The author does know the answer, so the question is a way to lead into the causes.$q$, 'draft', '814bbb48-1c10-56de-9ddf-22ab2d6ce631')
