   $q$Why does the author begin paragraph 2 with the word "Both"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It signals that the paragraph will explain what causes a team to win.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-signal"},{"text":"It signals that the paragraph will give the next step in a game.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-signal"},{"text":"It signals that the paragraph will tell ways the two sports are alike.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the author likes both sports exactly the same amount.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It signals that the paragraph will tell ways the two sports are alike.$q$, $q$"Both" is a signal word for likenesses, and paragraph 2 lists things the sports share, like passing and running. The author never tells which sport they like, so that choice is not supported.$q$, 'draft', 'f918bebd-4dd6-5d30-bd12-b940f4ba8f99')
